:: Nightclub - bathroom job [bg-nightclub]
<h1 class="ptitle">NIGHTCLUB</h1>
<br />
<<set _firstAsk = !($player?.quests?.gloryholeJobAsked ?? false)>>
/* One manager for every visit, so he looks the same when you come back to him */
<<if $game.gloryholeManager>>
    <<set $tmpGuy = $game.gloryholeManager>>
<<else>>
    <<newguy>>
    <<set $game.gloryholeManager = $tmpGuy>>
<</if>>
<<if _firstAsk>>
As you stood near the bar, taking in the sights and sounds of the underground city nightclub, a sudden presence at your side made you turn.
The man in the golden suit was there, almost as if he had materialized out of thin air. His approach was smooth and calculated, his steps deliberate as he closed the distance between you.
<br /><br />
<center>
    <<image 'places/nightclub/owner.jpg' sfw>>
</center>
<br />
With a charming smile, he extended a hand towards you, palm up as if offering a gift.
<br /><br />
<<sayNpc $tmpGuy>>
    My apologies for the abrupt introduction. I couldn't help but notice you. Word travels fast in these parts, especially when someone of your... reputation is involved.
<</sayNpc>>
<br />
The man in the golden suit gestured for you to follow him through the bustling underground city nightclub.
The neon lights flickered and cast an otherworldly glow over the scene as you wove through the crowd.
The air was thick with the scent of sweat, alcohol, and a hint of something metallic.
<br /><br />
<center>
    <<image 'places/nightclub/girl_dancing.webp' sfw>>
</center>
<br /><br />
As you entered a quieter section of the club, the man turned to you with a confident smile, his suit shimmering under the dim lights.
<br /><br />
<<sayNpc $tmpGuy>>
    I've heard about you. You have a way to get what you want, don't you?
<</sayNpc>>
<br />
You nodded cautiously, unsure of where this conversation was heading.
<br /><br />
<<else>>
You found the man in the golden suit near the bar, in the same spot where he had first approached you, and made your way through the crowd toward him.
He had already noticed you coming, and a slow, knowing smile spread across his face.
<br /><br />
<center>
    <<image 'places/nightclub/owner.jpg' sfw>>
</center>
<br />
<<sayNpc $tmpGuy>>
    Look who came back. Let me guess, you have reconsidered?
<</sayNpc>>
<br />
He nodded toward a quieter section of the club, and you followed him away from the thumping bass.
<br /><br />
<</if>>
<<sayNpc $tmpGuy>>
    Well, I have an offer for you. I have a luxurious bathroom in my establishment, one that would befit your girls. I could use some extra hands to attend to my guests.
<</sayNpc>>
<br />
<<sayNpc $tmpGuy>>
    Gloryholes.. I have few of them and my own girls are outdated so we could use fresh meat. So what are you saying?
<</sayNpc>>
<br />
His offer hung in the air, and you could sense the weight of the decision. On one hand, it was a chance for your girls to work in a more upscale environment, potentially earning more
and gaining a foothold in a different clientele. On the other hand, dealing with someone like this man could come with its own set of risks and complications.
<br /><br />
<<set $player.quests.gloryholeJobAsked = true>>
<div id="option_yes">
    <<linkreplace "Agree">>
        <<run $('#option_no').hide()>>
        <<set _agree = true>>
        <<set $player.quests.gloryholeJob = true>>
        <<set $player.goodwill -= 25>>
        <<sayNpc $tmpGuy>>
            Excellent! I will be waiting for your girls.
        <</sayNpc>>
        <br />
        You left the nightclub with a sense of optimism, knowing that your girls might have a chance at a more upscale and lucrative opportunity.
        <br /><br />
        <<link 'Leave'>>
            <<goto 'Nightclub - inside'>>
        <</link>>
    <</linkreplace>>
</div>
<div id="option_no">
    <<linkreplace "Do not agree">>
        <<run $('#option_yes').hide()>>
        <<if _firstAsk>>
            <<set $player.goodwill += 10>>
        <</if>>
        <<sayNpc $tmpGuy>>
            I respect your decision. Should you ever reconsider or need assistance of any kind, don't hesitate to reach out.
        <</sayNpc>>
        <br />
        You thanked him for his understanding and excused yourself, choosing to focus on your current operations rather than diving into a potentially risky partnership.
        <br /><br />
        <<link 'Leave'>>
            <<goto 'Nightclub - inside'>>
        <</link>>
    <</linkreplace>>
</div>

